@startuml
title History restoration: shallow node, deep node, and implicit re-entry
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Captured snapshot for scope s\nh(s) = (mode: deep, nodes: {Review, Screen})" as Snapshot #E7DCF5

state "Restore through a DEEP history node" as DeepCase #E9F5EA {
  state "history node (deep)" as DeepNode #E7DCF5
  state "Review" as ReviewD #DCEEFF
  state "Screen" as ScreenD #DCEEFF
  [*] --> DeepNode
  DeepNode --> ReviewD : accepts any remembered mode
  DeepNode --> ScreenD : one token per remembered node
}

state "Restore through a SHALLOW history node" as ShallowCase #FFF0D9 {
  state "history node (shallow)" as ShallowNode #E7DCF5
  state "declared initials" as InitialsS #DCEEFF
  [*] --> ShallowNode
  ShallowNode --> InitialsS : deep-recorded snapshot REFUSED\n/ fall back to initial nodes
}

state "Implicit re-entry through the owning scope node" as ImplicitCase #D9EFDF {
  state "scope node re-entered" as ScopeNode #ECF5FC
  state "remembered nodes" as RememberedI #DCEEFF
  [*] --> ScopeNode
  ScopeNode --> RememberedI : any nonempty history overrides\ninitials, with NO mode filter;\nentry activities re-run first
}

Snapshot -[#7D478F]-> DeepCase
Snapshot -[#7D478F]-> ShallowCase
Snapshot -[#7D478F]-> ImplicitCase

note bottom of ShallowCase #FFF3C9
Acceptance predicate for a history node of mode
<latex>m</latex> against snapshot <latex>h(s)</latex>:
<latex>\mathrm{accept}(m, h(s)) \equiv m = \mathtt{deep} \;\lor\; h(s).\mathrm{mode} = \mathtt{shallow}</latex>
Rejected, absent, or empty history falls back to the
scope's declared initial nodes.
end note
note right of Snapshot #EAF7EE
Capture happens only at scope completion and collapses
multiplicity: <latex>h(s) = \mathrm{keys}(\mathit{act}_{\sigma})</latex>.
The set holds each token's last recorded non-final
position, including positions of already-consumed tokens.
end note
@enduml
